DO NOT EDIT _skt_*.py
---------------------
These are byte-identical copies. Keeping them frozen is the whole point of this
layout: everything that has to change as upstream vLLM moves lives in our own
`model.py` / `__init__.py`, so a vLLM bump only touches vllm-rbln code, and when
SKT rebases their fork we can drop the new files in and delete the shims that are
no longer needed -- no three-way merge.

`ruff` is configured to skip `_skt_*.py` (see pyproject.toml). `ruff check --fix`
rewrote 12 places in _skt_model.py once; the exclude exists so tooling cannot
break the freeze again.

If a vLLM bump breaks these files, fix it in `model.py` (shim the upstream API
back into the shape the frozen file expects, or override the offending method).
Only give up and absorb the file into vllm-rbln proper when the adapter is
overriding more than ~3 axk2 methods or the shims exceed a few hundred lines --
at that point freezing costs more than owning.

The axk2 architecture is not in upstream vLLM yet; SKT's model card states
upstreaming is "in preparation". Everything under this directory is marked
REMOVE-WHEN-UPSTREAM: once a vLLM release ships axk2, `register_model()`
self-disables and this whole directory can be deleted.
